# .secret-scan-allow — documented false positives for
#   node scripts/scan-secrets.js --dir . --fail-on=high
#
# Format: `<pattern> | <reason>`. The pattern matches (case-insensitively)
# against the finding's file path or its rule label; `#` starts a comment.
# An entry WITHOUT a reason is a hard error (exit 2) — a false positive that
# nobody documented is a rule that quietly rots.
#
# Policy: never blanket-allow a first-party source directory. Vendored skill
# trees are allowed per subtree (they are third-party documentation whose job is
# to show API-key and shell examples). Our own hooks and scripts are allowed
# file-by-file, with the exact false positive named.

