# --- first-party: named false positives only --------------------------------
bundle/hooks/lib/phase-outcome.js | re.exec(blob) is a REGEX exec, not child_process — the scanner's exec() rule cannot tell them apart
bundle/opencode/hooks/lib/phase-outcome.js | mirror of bundle/hooks/lib/phase-outcome.js (regex exec, not child_process)
scripts/gen-agent-registry.js | frontmatter regex .exec(text) — same regex-exec false positive
scripts/test-agent-registry.js | suite builds the same regex .exec() fixtures the scanner rule matches
scripts/test-handshake-contract.js | suite builds the same regex .exec() fixtures the scanner rule matches
scripts/test-permission-review.js | suite builds the same regex .exec() fixtures the scanner rule matches
scripts/test-security-scanner.js | the scanner suite's own SYNTHETIC secret fixtures (ghp_/AKIA/password shapes) — they must exist to test detection
scripts/setup-cursor-byok.sh | OPENAI_API_KEY="$provider_key" is a shell variable expansion read from an interactive prompt, not a stored secret
docs/audit/agent-architecture-audit.md | the audit report quotes the scanner's own rule regexes (eval(, Stripe/GitHub/AWS key shapes)